  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Plays one frame of music. The frame-end raster IRQ calls it at $29bf. game_mode is the tune: 0 silences the SID, a new value starts that tune."},
    {"at":2,"placement":"side","text":"game_mode 0 silences the SID; no run executed this"},
    {"at":15,"placement":"line","text":"Same tune: writes volume, resonance and cutoff base to the SID, then steps the voices."},
    {"at":42,"placement":"line","text":"Starts tune A: resets the SID and the voices, sets volume and tempo, and copies the pattern base, pattern table and order lists. It does not play in this frame."},
    {"at":53,"placement":"side","text":"$81: voice on, bit 7 = write the SID registers"},
    {"at":109,"placement":"side","text":"Patches the operands of $0ad0 and $0adc with the pattern offset table"},
    {"at":127,"placement":"side","text":"The high byte of the offset is at table+1"},
    {"at":172,"placement":"line","text":"Steps voices 2 to 0. A voice reads its order list and pattern when its tempo counter reaches 0. In the other frames only its frequency changes."},
    {"at":210,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the order list command at music_order_pos and jumps through music_order_commands: 0 stop, 1 pattern, 2 jump, 3 repeat."},
    {"at":230,"placement":"side","text":"Command handler from music_order_commands"},
    {"at":233,"placement":"line","text":"Frequency of this frame: a slide instrument moves toward the note frequency, other instruments get the note frequency at once."},
    {"at":259,"placement":"side","text":"After the voices: modulators, pulse widths, filter cutoff"},
    {"at":289,"placement":"line","text":"Order command 1, pattern: on a new entry it sets the pattern address (offset + music_pattern_base) and reads the first byte. Else the note counts down."},
    {"at":299,"placement":"side","text":"Self-modified: low byte of the pattern offset"},
    {"at":311,"placement":"side","text":"Self-modified: high byte of the pattern offset"},
    {"at":333,"placement":"line","text":"Counts the note down. At 0 the note gets one release tick with the gate off. Duration flag bit 6 keeps the gate on."},
    {"at":354,"placement":"side","text":"Flag bit 6 keeps the gate on through the release tick"},
    {"at":372,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the next pattern byte: $ff ends the pattern, $80-$fe selects an instrument, other values start a note of two bytes."},
    {"at":382,"placement":"side","text":"$ff: end of pattern, next order entry"},
    {"at":400,"placement":"side","text":"$80-$fe: instrument number"},
    {"at":408,"placement":"line","text":"Note byte: bits 0-3 note (0 rest, 1-12 C to B), bits 4-6 octave. Frequency = (music_note_freqs + $100) << (octave + instrument octave)."},
    {"at":440,"placement":"side","text":"Octave of the note plus the octave offset of the instrument"},
    {"at":458,"placement":"line","text":"Duration byte: bits 0-3 index music_durations, bits 6-7 go to music_note_flags. A note lasts the table value + 1 ticks."},
    {"at":458,"placement":"side","text":"Y is always 0 here, thus the release flag clears"},
    {"at":480,"placement":"side","text":"Index 14 skips the release tick; no run executed this"},
    {"at":487,"placement":"line","text":"If the previous note had flags, the current frequency stays. Thus a slide instrument glides into the new note."},
    {"at":510,"placement":"side","text":"A rest leaves the gate as it is"}
  ],
